From: moulton@netcom.com (Fred C. Moulton)
Date: Fri, 7 Oct 1994 23:11:25 -0700
Subject: [#94-10-136] M.S. in Studies of the Future from UHCL

I think that Nick overstates the case somewhat about futurists.  While
it is correct that some futurists are similar to what he describes, it is
also correct to observe that not all are Fabian socialists.  I am not.

Nor are all futurists blindly extrapolating current trends into the future.
For example one of the developers of the Delphi polling method was Harold
Linstone, professor emeritus at Portland State University.  This and many
other methods are used by futurists, some more successfully than others.
One of the most well known of the misapplication of extrapolation is the
Club of Rome study which has been recognized as flawed by the futurist
community.

And let us not forget that sometimes extrapolating a trend is a useful
activity.

Fred

